                <pb facs="0829" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg709"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.12 Gomez and Rubio/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Clark</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-08T18:00:00-04:00">June 8, 1931—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>164. Please transmit the following message to President Ortiz Rubio, on behalf of
                    the President: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>I have just learned with deep regret of the report that two Mexican
                            students, one of them a relative of Your Excellency, were killed this
                            morning at Ardmore, Oklahoma. I have ordered a minute investigation of
                            the circumstances of this profoundly regrettable
                    incident.</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
